{"content":[{"c":["BITUMEN*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Asphalt as found in its natural state; pitch, tar. “Bitumen” (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “slime”) was used for mortar in the Tower of Babel’s construction (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.11.3","r":"Gen.11.3","rawR":"Gen.11.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.11.3","value":"Gen.11.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 11:3"},") and to seal the reed basket in which baby Moses was concealed (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.2.3","r":"Exod.2.3","rawR":"Exod.2.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.2.3","value":"Exod.2.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 2:3"},"). In Israel, the valley of Siddim was dotted with numerous bitumen pits into which a number of soldiers fell during Chedorlaomer’s war against Sodom and Gomorrah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.10","r":"Gen.14.10","rawR":"Gen.14.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.10","value":"Gen.14.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:10"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Asphalt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Asphalt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Asphalt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Asphalt"},"; ",{"href":"?item=MineralsandMetals_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MineralsandMetals_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MineralsandMetals_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Minerals and Metals"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Bitumen","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 11:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.11.3","rawQueryValue":"Gen.11.3","sourceRefExact":"Gen.11.3"},{"anchorText":"Ex 2:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.2.3","rawQueryValue":"Exod.2.3","sourceRefExact":"Exod.2.3"},{"anchorText":"Gn 14:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.10","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.10","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.10"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5f6818f32708abab7a5e10f8446a086a66e546e3a47347bb2f1038f24adde609","sourceItemName":"Bitumen","sourceItemOrder":337,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Bitumen","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Bitumen*","title":"Bitumen*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}